b-information-sheet","verified":"Close and regular contact with an infectious person is generally needed for transmission.","quality_score":"4","adoption":"TB_02","direct_score_input":false},{"row":133,"status":"PASS_TB_03","source":"UKHSA tuberculosis public information","url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/tuberculosis-tb-factsheet/tuberculosis-tb-information-sheet","verified":"Active TB can cause symptoms, illness and onward transmission.","quality_score":"4","adoption":"TB_03","direct_score_input":false},{"row":134,"status":"PASS_TB_04","source":"UKHSA tuberculosis public information","url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/tuberculosis-tb-factsheet/tuberculosis-tb-information-sheet","verified":"Symptoms can include a persistent cough, blood in phlegm, fever, night sweats, weight loss and extreme tiredness.","quality_score":"4","adoption":"TB_04","direct_score_input":false},{"row":135,"status":"PASS_TB_05","source":"UKHSA tuberculosis public information","url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/tuberculosis-tb-factsheet/tuberculosis-tb-information-sheet","verified":"Latent TB has no symptoms and cannot be passed to other people.","quality_score":"4","adoption":"TB_05","direct_score_input":false},{"row":136,"status":"PASS_TB_06","source":"UKHSA tuberculosis public information","url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/tuberculosis-tb-factsheet/tuberculosis-tb-information-sheet","verified":"TB testing can include chest X-ray, skin testing, blood testing and phlegm samples.","quality_score":"4","adoption":"TB_06","direct_score_input":false},{"row":137,"status":"PASS_TB_07","source":"UKHSA tuberculosis public information","url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/tuberculosis-tb-factsheet/tuberculosis-tb-information-sheet","verified":"Anyone can develop TB, with higher likelihood associated with close contact, weakened immunity, overcrowding and previous inadequately treated TB.","quality_score":"4","adoption":"TB_07",